       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That's double the labeled maximum daily dose of 2,550 mg for immediate-release metformin in adults. At that dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up, and kidney and liver function being normal doesn't change that.\n\nThis may be a typo. These are some options that stay within the label:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, which is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **500 mg to 850 mg PO two or three times daily**, if you're starting or titrating.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you really do intend a dose above the labeled maximum, it will need to go through pharmacy or the prescriber, and I can't enter it."
      }
